>> title: Boba Pearls
>> servings: 4
>> author: Ted Lin
>> date: 2020-03-17
>> dish: boba
>> cuisine: Taiwanese
>> course: drink
>> keywords: tapioca, milk tea
>> summary: Homemade tapioca pearls in brown sugar syrup, with milk tea; best made a day ahead.
>> image: static/photos/boba-pearls/cupotea.jpg
>> image: static/photos/boba-pearls/balls.jpg
>> image: static/photos/boba-pearls/boiling.jpg
>> image: static/photos/boba-pearls/bobasyrup.jpg
>> image: static/photos/boba-pearls/milktea.jpg
>> source: https://www.chinasichuanfood.com/how-to-make-boba-pearls-at-home/
>> source: https://thewoksoflife.com/how-to-cook-tapioca-pearls/
>> source: https://www.foxyfolksy.com/how-to-make-black-tapioca-pearls/

# Pearls

:heat @{water|6 tbsp}, @{dark brown sugar|4 tbsp} in #pot until dissolved => _syrup.
:mix @{tapioca flour|1/3 cup} into _syrup QUICKLY until smooth => _paste.
  (if you wait, it clumps and needs extra mashing)
:fold _paste into @{tapioca flour|2/3 cup} on a work surface with #scraper until mostly incorporated or cool enough to handle, then knead until all the flour is absorbed => _dough.
  (it stays a little tacky; resist adding more flour)
:roll _dough in chunks into cylinders, at most 1 cm in diameter => _cylinders.
  (the cylinder size sets the pearl size; go smaller if you want them straw-able)
:cut _cylinders into pieces and round into rough spheres => _pearls.
:dust _pearls lightly with @flour.
  (they keep a day in the fridge, or freeze)

# Cook

:boil @{water|a lot} in #{large pot} to a rolling boil => _{boiling water}.
  (more than you think you need; the pearls release a lot of starch)
:{simmer|15 min} _pearls in _{boiling water} in #{pot|lid on}.
:{rest|15 min} _pearls off the heat in #{pot|lid on} => _{cooked pearls}.
  (if still doughy, drain, rinse in cold water, and repeat the cooking)

# Syrup

:dissolve @{water|4 tbsp}, @{dark brown sugar|1/3 cup} in #pot over low-medium heat => _{brown sugar syrup}.
  (start while the pearls cook)
:drain _{cooked pearls} and combine with _{brown sugar syrup} => _{syrup pearls}.
  (these keep in the fridge for a few days)

# Milk tea

:heat @{black tea|loose leaf} with @{milk|several cups} in #pot over low heat until the milk is steaming => _tea.
:brew _tea off the heat to taste; longer is stronger.
:serve _tea chilled or over lots of ice with _{syrup pearls}.

>> note: Very sweet, usually too sweet.
>> note: Also good with equal parts coffee and milk instead of tea.
